-- title:
--   Newvector conductor at q of a weight-one primitive form's adelic span
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, $\psi$ a Dirichlet character modulo $N$ with values in $\mathbb{C}$, and $f$ a cusp form of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(N)$ which is a primitive form with nebentypus $\psi$, i.e. $f$ is an eigenform in the sense that its first $q$-expansion coefficient is $1$, that $\mathrm{qCoeff}\,f(pn)+\psi(p)p^{0}\cdot[\,p\mid n\,]\,\mathrm{qCoeff}\,f(n/p)=\mathrm{qCoeff}\,f(p)\,\mathrm{qCoeff}\,f(n)$ for all primes $p\nmid N$ and all $n$, that $\mathrm{qCoeff}\,f(\ell n)=\mathrm{qCoeff}\,f(\ell)\,\mathrm{qCoeff}\,f(n)$ for all primes $\ell\mid N$ and all $n$, and that $f$ has nebentypus $\psi$, and moreover for every proper divisor $M'$ of $N$ the eigenpacket given by the coefficients of $f$ and the values of $\psi$ does not occur in weight $1$ at level $M'$. Let $q$ be a prime. Form $\varphi_f=\mathrm{weightOneLift}$ of $f$ at the ideal $(N)\subseteq\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$: at an adelic point $g$ admitting a decomposition $g=\gamma\,h\,u$ with $\gamma$ rational, $u$ in the level-$(N)$ compact open subgroup, $h$ having trivial finite part and totally positive archimedean part, the value is $(f\mid[1]h_\infty)(i)\cdot\det(h_\infty)$ for the archimedean realisation $h_\infty$ of such an $h$, and $0$ if no such decomposition exists. Let $V$ be the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the right translates $g\cdot\varphi_f$, $g\in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$, inside the carrier of adelic functions, viewed as a $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-module. The conclusion is that $V$ has newvector conductor $v_q(N)=$ `N.factorization q` at $q$: the subspace of vectors of $V$ fixed by $K_1(q^{v_q(N)})\subseteq\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ is nonzero, while for every $m<v_q(N)$ the subspace fixed by $K_1(q^m)$ is zero.
--
--   This is the local conductor statement of Casselman's theory of newvectors, in the weight-one $\Gamma_1(N)$ setting, transported through the classical-to-adelic dictionary: the local component at $q$ of the automorphic representation generated by a primitive form of level $N$ has conductor exponent $v_q(N)$. It feeds the construction of a genuine cuspidal realisation with prescribed newvector conductors attached to a weight-one primitive form.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DihedralWeightOne_hasNewvectorConductor_adelicSpan_weightOneLift_factorization_of_isPrimitiveForm.lean

